* QtSpice sample library: 1 MHz peak-current-mode synchronous buck (examples/buck_cpm)
*
* Hand-written for QtSpice. It follows the behaviour of the gate driver, dead-time and
* CPM modulator models used in the CU Boulder power electronics course, rebuilt from
* elements ngspice and QtSpice support (R C L V E G D M X): logic is CMOS inverters and
* MOSFET switches, comparators are high-gain E-sources with diode clamps. No vendor
* models. Instance parameters are fixed here (QtSpice 0.2 does not pass parameters
* into symbols): edit the .param lines to change them.

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- logic primitives
.model qs_nl NMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=1 KP=2m)
.model qs_pl PMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=-1 KP=2m)
.model qs_d D (IS=1f N=1)

* CMOS inverter: in -> out, powered from vdd/vss
.subckt qs_inv in out vdd vss
Mp out in vdd vdd qs_pl
Mn out in vss vss qs_nl
Cout out vss 0.1p
.ends qs_inv

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- dead_time
* c: PWM input (0/5 V). c1 = c with its rising edge delayed by Td, c2 = not c with its
* rising edge delayed by Td: two complementary, non-overlapping 0/5 V signals.
.subckt dead_time c c1 c2
.param Td=30n
Vdd vdd 0 5
X1 c cn vdd 0 qs_inv
X2 cn cc vdd 0 qs_inv
R1 cc cd 1k
C1 cd 0 {Td/693}
D1 cd cc qs_d
X3 cd c1n vdd 0 qs_inv
X4 c1n c1 vdd 0 qs_inv
X5 c cb vdd 0 qs_inv
R2 cb cbd 1k
C2 cbd 0 {Td/693}
D2 cbd cb qs_d
X6 cbd c2n vdd 0 qs_inv
X7 c2n c2 vdd 0 qs_inv
.ends dead_time

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- driver
* Gate driver for a low-side or (bootstrapped) high-side MOSFET.
* c: 0/5 V control referred to Vssin; out swings Vss..Vdd; RC propagation delay Tdelay.
* (The undervoltage lockout of the course model is not modelled.)
.subckt driver c Vdd Vss Vssin out
.param Tdelay=20n IQ=1m Imax=3
.param VT=2 Vddrated=12
.param Rdelay=100
E1 ciso Vss c Vssin 1
R1 ciso cdel {Rdelay}
C1 cdel Vss {Tdelay/Rdelay/0.69}
X1 cdel gate Vdd Vss qs_inv
M1 out gate Vdd Vdd drv_p
M2 out gate Vss Vss drv_n
Ibias Vdd Vss {IQ}
.model drv_n NMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO={VT} KP={2*Imax/(Vddrated-VT)/(Vddrated-VT)})
.model drv_p PMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO={-VT} KP={1.4*Imax/(Vddrated-VT)/(Vddrated-VT)})
.ends driver

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- CPM_modulator
* Peak current mode modulator. A clock sets the latch at the start of each period; the
* latch resets when vs + Voffset + ramp reaches the limited control voltage vc, or at
* Dmax. PWM is the 0/5 V latch output; ramp is the artificial ramp.
* Va = 0 (no slope compensation), as in the original example: at D > 0.5 this gives
* subharmonic oscillation of the inductor current. Va=0.3 removes it.
.subckt CPM_modulator vc vs PWM ramp
.param fs=1meg Va=0 Vcmax=0.8 Dmin=0 Dmax=0.95 Voffset=1
Vdd vdd 0 5
Vmid mid 0 2.5
* control input, limited to about 0 .. Vcmax+Voffset
Rin vc 0 10meg
Rb vc b 1k
Vlim lim 0 {Vcmax+Voffset-0.55}
Dlim b lim qs_d
Dneg 0 b qs_d
* current signal plus offset and artificial ramp
Varamp a vs PULSE({Voffset} {Voffset+Va} 0 {0.99/fs} {0.01/fs} 0 {1/fs})
E1 ramp 0 a vs 1
* comparator: comp high when a > b
Ecmp x mid a b 1000
Rcmp x y 100k
Dch y vdd qs_d
Dcl 0 y qs_d
X1 y yn vdd 0 qs_inv
X2 yn comp vdd 0 qs_inv
* set clock (narrow pulse at the start of each period) and Dmax reset
Vclk clk 0 PULSE(0 5 0 1n 1n {Dmin/fs+5n} {1/fs})
Vclk_Dmax clk_dmax 0 PULSE(0 5 {Dmax/fs} 1n 1n {(1-Dmax)/fs-2n} {1/fs})
* latch: q held by a weak feedback resistor; set pulls q up, reset (stronger) pulls down
Eset gs vdd clk 0 -1
Mset q gs vdd vdd qs_ps
Mr1 q comp 0 0 qs_ns
Mr2 q clk_dmax 0 0 qs_ns
Cq q 0 1p
X3 q qn vdd 0 qs_inv
X4 qn PWM vdd 0 qs_inv
Rfb PWM q 5k
.model qs_ps PMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=-1 KP=5m)
.model qs_ns NMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=1 KP=20m)
.ends CPM_modulator

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- error amplifier
* Generic op-amp: 100 dB DC gain, 30 MHz gain-bandwidth, output clamped near the rails.
* Pins as the QtSpice built-in opamp symbol: In+ In- V+ V- OUT.
.subckt ea_opamp inp inn vcc vee out
Rin inp inn 10meg
G1 vee n1 inp inn 1m
R1 n1 vee 100meg
C1 n1 vee {1m/(2*3.14159265*30meg)}
Dh n1 vcc qs_d
Dl vee n1 qs_d
E1 o vee n1 vee 1
Rout o out 10
.ends ea_opamp

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- power devices
* Generic 30 V logic-level power NMOS (pins d g s): about 15 mOhm at Vgs = 4.5 V,
* 1 nF gate-source and 0.2 nF gate-drain capacitance, the drain-bulk junction as the body
* diode, and a 100 pF linear output capacitance (Coss), which also keeps the switch node
* well behaved for the ngspice time step control.
.subckt nfet_pwr d g s
M1 d g s s nmos_pwr
Coss d s 100p
.model nmos_pwr NMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=1.7 KP=25 IS=1e-12 CGSO=10u CGDO=2u RD=1m RS=1m)
.ends nfet_pwr
* Generic 1 A Schottky diode
.model schottky_1a D (IS=10u N=1.2 RS=50m CJO=100p)
